Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: spread the tiler's hierarchy levels out when the
 GPU has fewer than 8

pan_select_tiler_hierarchy_mask() gave a GPU with fewer than 8 hierarchy
levels the coarsest ones only. The RG DS's Mali-G52 has 2 (dmesg: Tiler
0x209), so the bins were 256 and 512 pixels on the RG DS's 640x480 panels
and 512 and 1024 pixels on the RG DS Plus's 1024x768: every small triangle
was looked at by every tile of half a screen or more, and a scene of many
small triangles is slow (BananaLinux issue #316: about 2000 triangles of
a program's own UI, 16 ms of GPU time a frame on the RG DS Plus).

Mesa 25.2 spreads the levels out instead: with 2 levels, 32-pixel bins and
one that covers the framebuffer (mask 0x82). A GPU with 8 levels or more
gets the same mask as before.

Backport to 25.0.7 of what Mesa 25.2.0 has in
GENX(pan_select_tiler_hierarchy_mask), src/panfrost/lib/pan_desc.c (upstream
commit 548f652d101f; in 25.0 the function is in pan_util.h and has no tile
size or memory budget to look at).
---
 src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h
--- a/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/pan_util.h
@@ -85,7 +85,19 @@
 {
    uint32_t max_fb_wh = MAX2(width, height);
    uint32_t last_hierarchy_bit = util_last_bit(DIV_ROUND_UP(max_fb_wh, 16));
-   uint32_t hierarchy_mask = BITFIELD_MASK(max_levels);
+   uint32_t hierarchy_mask;
+
+   if (max_levels < 8) {
+      /* spread the bits out somewhat */
+      static uint32_t default_mask[] = {
+         0, 0x80, 0x82, 0xa2,
+         0xaa, 0xea, 0xee, 0xfe
+      };
+      hierarchy_mask = default_mask[max_levels];
+      max_levels = 8; /* the high bit of the mask is always set */
+   } else {
+      hierarchy_mask = BITFIELD_MASK(max_levels);
+   }
 
    /* Always enable the level covering the whole FB, and disable the finest
     * levels if we don't have enough to cover everything.
